{
  "stage": "extract",
  "item": "__OiQznq4ao",
  "inputs_hash": "871f23743daae372c746f390ed4bc2c7387ebefd049c08dab5bf8ea215f4bda9",
  "output_hash": "5fe24f98305e28e5f9c15b1bcb6a6ce0e390c665c00f04b5a5ea5eda17439bc1",
  "output": {
    "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
    "points": [
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p001",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 1,
        "text": "This lecture covers step four of the instruction fine-tuning hands-on project, which is loading a pre-trained large language model.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@13",
          "__OiQznq4ao@16",
          "__OiQznq4ao@18",
          "__OiQznq4ao@20",
          "__OiQznq4ao@23"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p002",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The dataset used for instruction fine-tuning has 1,100 entries of instructions, inputs, and outputs from various fields, and its purpose is to teach the LLM to follow instructions correctly.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@35",
          "__OiQznq4ao@37",
          "__OiQznq4ao@41",
          "__OiQznq4ao@44",
          "__OiQznq4ao@47",
          "__OiQznq4ao@53"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p003",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Fine-tuning here means training a pre-trained LLM on a specific dataset so that it follows instructions better, because a pre-trained LLM by itself does not follow instructions very well.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@58",
          "__OiQznq4ao@60",
          "__OiQznq4ao@63",
          "__OiQznq4ao@66",
          "__OiQznq4ao@68",
          "__OiQznq4ao@70"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p004",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Before loading a pre-trained LLM, the workflow required downloading the dataset, converting it into the Alpaca prompt style, batching it, and creating data loaders.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@73",
          "__OiQznq4ao@76",
          "__OiQznq4ao@79",
          "__OiQznq4ao@81",
          "__OiQznq4ao@84",
          "__OiQznq4ao@87",
          "__OiQznq4ao@89",
          "__OiQznq4ao@90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p005",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Loading a pre-trained LLM means taking the LLM architecture and filling its trainable weights with previously trained weights.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@94",
          "__OiQznq4ao@96",
          "__OiQznq4ao@98",
          "__OiQznq4ao@101",
          "__OiQznq4ao@104",
          "__OiQznq4ao@106"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p006",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The trainable parts of the model include the query, key, and value weights in multi-head attention, the weights in the feed-forward network, the scale and shift parameters in layer normalization, and the token and positional embedding layers.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@106",
          "__OiQznq4ao@111",
          "__OiQznq4ao@116",
          "__OiQznq4ao@120",
          "__OiQznq4ao@124",
          "__OiQznq4ao@129"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p007",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The model contains more than 1 million or more than 100 million trainable parameters when all of these trainable weights are added together.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@130",
          "__OiQznq4ao@133",
          "__OiQznq4ao@134",
          "__OiQznq4ao@136"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p008",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "In pre-training, these parameters are trained on a huge amount of data.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@138",
          "__OiQznq4ao@140",
          "__OiQznq4ao@142"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p009",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "OpenAI pre-trained GPT-2, optimized its trainable weights, and released those weights publicly so that users can access and use them.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@145",
          "__OiQznq4ao@149",
          "__OiQznq4ao@152",
          "__OiQznq4ao@155",
          "__OiQznq4ao@160",
          "__OiQznq4ao@165",
          "__OiQznq4ao@170",
          "__OiQznq4ao@172"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p010",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "OpenAI released GPT-2 weights for multiple model sizes, including 124 million, 345 million, 774 million, and 1558 million parameters, and the weights can be downloaded from folders corresponding to those parameter sizes.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@174",
          "__OiQznq4ao@176",
          "__OiQznq4ao@178",
          "__OiQznq4ao@183",
          "__OiQznq4ao@192",
          "__OiQznq4ao@196",
          "__OiQznq4ao@198"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p011",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The reason for downloading and reusing pre-trained weights before fine-tuning is that they already capture a lot of useful information, such as semantic structure in token embeddings, and training the whole network again from scratch would take much longer and require more computation.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@203",
          "__OiQznq4ao@205",
          "__OiQznq4ao@211",
          "__OiQznq4ao@217",
          "__OiQznq4ao@224",
          "__OiQznq4ao@228",
          "__OiQznq4ao@232",
          "__OiQznq4ao@234"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p012",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Reusing GPT-2 weights helps because the model starts from a much more knowledgeable state instead of a random initialization.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@236",
          "__OiQznq4ao@241",
          "__OiQznq4ao@244",
          "__OiQznq4ao@247",
          "__OiQznq4ao@251",
          "__OiQznq4ao@253",
          "__OiQznq4ao@257",
          "__OiQznq4ao@261",
          "__OiQznq4ao@273",
          "__OiQznq4ao@283"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p013",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The process is to load the pre-trained weights first and then train on the curated dataset using the training, testing, and validation data loaders.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@283",
          "__OiQznq4ao@285",
          "__OiQznq4ao@287",
          "__OiQznq4ao@289",
          "__OiQznq4ao@291",
          "__OiQznq4ao@293",
          "__OiQznq4ao@296"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p014",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "During fine-tuning, the weights loaded from GPT-2 will still change, but starting from a knowledgeable state makes training on the specific dataset much more efficient and lower in computational time.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@298",
          "__OiQznq4ao@300",
          "__OiQznq4ao@302",
          "__OiQznq4ao@306",
          "__OiQznq4ao@308",
          "__OiQznq4ao@311",
          "__OiQznq4ao@313",
          "__OiQznq4ao@316",
          "__OiQznq4ao@318",
          "__OiQznq4ao@320"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p015",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Fine-tuning happens after pre-training because pre-training first brings the model to a knowledgeable state, after which training on a specific dataset further improves its weights and parameters.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@320",
          "__OiQznq4ao@324",
          "__OiQznq4ao@327",
          "__OiQznq4ao@330",
          "__OiQznq4ao@332",
          "__OiQznq4ao@335"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p016",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "For this instruction fine-tuning task, the lecturer uses GPT-2 medium with 355 million parameters because the smaller 124 million parameter model did not perform very well.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@343",
          "__OiQznq4ao@346",
          "__OiQznq4ao@350",
          "__OiQznq4ao@355",
          "__OiQznq4ao@358",
          "__OiQznq4ao@361",
          "__OiQznq4ao@366",
          "__OiQznq4ao@371",
          "__OiQznq4ao@375",
          "__OiQznq4ao@378"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p017",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Using GPT-2 medium with 355 million parameters requires about 1.42 GB of storage space on the local machine.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@390",
          "__OiQznq4ao@392",
          "__OiQznq4ao@395",
          "__OiQznq4ao@398",
          "__OiQznq4ao@402",
          "__OiQznq4ao@406"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p018",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The GPT-2 medium configuration has context size 1024, 24 transformer blocks, and 16 attention heads in each transformer block.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@419",
          "__OiQznq4ao@423",
          "__OiQznq4ao@425",
          "__OiQznq4ao@428",
          "__OiQznq4ao@431",
          "__OiQznq4ao@435",
          "__OiQznq4ao@437"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p019",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "In the base configuration, the vocabulary size is 50,257, the context length is 1024, the dropout rate is zero, and the query-key-value bias is set to true so that the bias terms are also initialized.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@443",
          "__OiQznq4ao@445",
          "__OiQznq4ao@448",
          "__OiQznq4ao@452",
          "__OiQznq4ao@455",
          "__OiQznq4ao@457",
          "__OiQznq4ao@459",
          "__OiQznq4ao@463"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p020",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The value 50,257 is the vocabulary size on which GPT-2 was trained.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@463",
          "__OiQznq4ao@467",
          "__OiQznq4ao@469"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p021",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The download_and_load_gpt2 function downloads seven files from a URL to the local machine and then preprocesses them.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@472",
          "__OiQznq4ao@474",
          "__OiQznq4ao@476",
          "__OiQznq4ao@481",
          "__OiQznq4ao@484",
          "__OiQznq4ao@487",
          "__OiQznq4ao@490",
          "__OiQznq4ao@503",
          "__OiQznq4ao@505"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p022",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Simply downloading the seven files is not enough, because they must be converted from the TensorFlow checkpoint into a specific dictionary format so the parameters can be handled more easily.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@501",
          "__OiQznq4ao@503",
          "__OiQznq4ao@505",
          "__OiQznq4ao@507",
          "__OiQznq4ao@510",
          "__OiQznq4ao@513",
          "__OiQznq4ao@518",
          "__OiQznq4ao@520",
          "__OiQznq4ao@524",
          "__OiQznq4ao@526"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p023",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Running the code creates a folder called 355M, downloads the seven files, and returns a params dictionary containing transformer block parameters, token embeddings, positional embeddings, and final normalization layer parameters in an accessible form.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@538",
          "__OiQznq4ao@540",
          "__OiQznq4ao@542",
          "__OiQznq4ao@545",
          "__OiQznq4ao@548",
          "__OiQznq4ao@550",
          "__OiQznq4ao@554",
          "__OiQznq4ao@556",
          "__OiQznq4ao@557",
          "__OiQznq4ao@560",
          "__OiQznq4ao@562"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p024",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Creating the params dictionary is essential because directly using the seven downloaded files makes it difficult to integrate the parameters with the previously written GPT code.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@562",
          "__OiQznq4ao@564",
          "__OiQznq4ao@567",
          "__OiQznq4ao@568",
          "__OiQznq4ao@570",
          "__OiQznq4ao@573",
          "__OiQznq4ao@576"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p025",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "code",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The code imports the download_and_load_gpt2 function from the GPT_download3.py file and stores its results in settings and params.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@586",
          "__OiQznq4ao@588",
          "__OiQznq4ao@595",
          "__OiQznq4ao@598",
          "__OiQznq4ao@602",
          "__OiQznq4ao@606",
          "__OiQznq4ao@608"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p026",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Downloading the 1.42 GB model can take a long time, so it helps to have strong internet and enough memory on the device.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@611",
          "__OiQznq4ao@614",
          "__OiQznq4ao@617",
          "__OiQznq4ao@620",
          "__OiQznq4ao@623",
          "__OiQznq4ao@628",
          "__OiQznq4ao@630",
          "__OiQznq4ao@632",
          "__OiQznq4ao@635",
          "__OiQznq4ao@640"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p027",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The load_weights_into_gpt function maps the downloaded parameters from the params dictionary into the corresponding trainable parts of the GPT architecture.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@643",
          "__OiQznq4ao@645",
          "__OiQznq4ao@646",
          "__OiQznq4ao@649",
          "__OiQznq4ao@652",
          "__OiQznq4ao@656",
          "__OiQznq4ao@658",
          "__OiQznq4ao@661",
          "__OiQznq4ao@673",
          "__OiQznq4ao@678",
          "__OiQznq4ao@680"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p028",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "analogy",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The whole code block for loading weights can be thought of as an assignment step that assigns the downloaded parameters to the model.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@700",
          "__OiQznq4ao@703",
          "__OiQznq4ao@705",
          "__OiQznq4ao@707",
          "__OiQznq4ao@709",
          "__OiQznq4ao@711",
          "__OiQznq4ao@713",
          "__OiQznq4ao@715"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p029",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "After running settings, params = download_and_load_gpt2, the next step is to run load_weights_into_gpt to load the downloaded 355 million parameter weights into the GPT architecture and then set the model to evaluation mode.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@725",
          "__OiQznq4ao@727",
          "__OiQznq4ao@728",
          "__OiQznq4ao@731",
          "__OiQznq4ao@733",
          "__OiQznq4ao@736",
          "__OiQznq4ao@738"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p030",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "If a laptop has limited memory or processing speed, GPT-2 small with 124 million parameters can be used instead, and it should take about one-third to one-half as much time to load as GPT-2 medium.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@738",
          "__OiQznq4ao@741",
          "__OiQznq4ao@745",
          "__OiQznq4ao@747",
          "__OiQznq4ao@750",
          "__OiQznq4ao@751",
          "__OiQznq4ao@754",
          "__OiQznq4ao@756"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p031",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "If a laptop has high processing speed and GPU access, GPT-2 large or GPT-2 XL can be used, and they should give much better results than smaller models.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@759",
          "__OiQznq4ao@761",
          "__OiQznq4ao@763",
          "__OiQznq4ao@766",
          "__OiQznq4ao@768",
          "__OiQznq4ao@771",
          "__OiQznq4ao@772",
          "__OiQznq4ao@776"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p032",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 1,
        "text": "If the GPT-2 parameters have already been downloaded, the output will indicate that the files already exist.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@778",
          "__OiQznq4ao@781",
          "__OiQznq4ao@783",
          "__OiQznq4ao@786",
          "__OiQznq4ao@788"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p033",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Before fine-tuning, you can evaluate the pre-trained LLM on a validation example by comparing its output to the expected response, even though the model has not yet been trained on the instruction dataset.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@790",
          "__OiQznq4ao@792",
          "__OiQznq4ao@795",
          "__OiQznq4ao@797",
          "__OiQznq4ao@799",
          "__OiQznq4ao@802",
          "__OiQznq4ao@804",
          "__OiQznq4ao@806",
          "__OiQznq4ao@809"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "__OiQznq4ao:p034",
        "video_id": "__OiQznq4ao",
        "lecture": 40,
        "kind": "visual_ref",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The lecturer selects a validation example whose instruction is to convert the active sentence \"The chef cooks the meal every day\" into the passive voice.",
        "line_ids": [
          "__OiQznq4ao@816",
          "__OiQznq4ao@818",
          "__OiQznq4ao@820",
          "__OiQznq4ao@822",
